Ilmari Karonen wrote:
> Doug Freyburger <dfreybur@yahoo.com> wrote:
>>
>> If MC were handled per armor item that would sure give further advantage
>> to mirthril!  Yet it would be one of those features that tempts people
>> without being worth it in the long run.
>
> If wearing an MC3 cloak over mithril gave you something like the
> equivalent of MC 9 = 3*3 (and if MC was nerfed in general as proposed,
> so that going above 3 would actually matter), then it seems to me that
> mithril + AoR (or SoR) + CoMR could become a viable ascension kit
> choice, at least for non-spellcasters.

It would be nice for the MC code to run once per layer of armor that has
it, but would this change matter enough to make it worth it?  Except for
some sort of super-kraken speculation the types of attack handled by MC
aren't really worth the difference in AC to me.  It would be a
temptation not a solution.  Do added temptations add game balance?  Not
to well spoiled or well experienced players and I think most of the
discussion here is intended to address them not beginners.


